      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the pain and redness persist despite ibuprofen, you may consider alternative options. Aspirin can also help with inflammation, but it's generally recommended to avoid it with bleeding disorders or in people who are prone to stomach issues. You may also consider taking a stronger anti-inflammatory like naproxen or diclofenac, but always follow the recommended dosage and consult a doctor or pharmacist before taking any new medication.",
